# To-Do List App

## Stack

- Plain **HTML**, **CSS**, and **JavaScript** only — no frameworks, bundlers, or backend
- Three files at repo root: `index.html`, `styles.css`, `app.js`
- Open `index.html` directly in a browser; no build step required

## Architecture

- **State**: in-memory `tasks` array in `app.js`
- **Task shape**: `{ id, text, priority, dueDate, completed }`
  - `dueDate`: ISO date string (`YYYY-MM-DD`) or `null` if unset
  - `id`: `crypto.randomUUID()`
  - `priority`: `"high" | "medium" | "low"` (lowercase, matches `<select>` values and CSS classes)
- **UI updates**: single `render()` rebuilds the list and refreshes counters after every change

## Features to preserve

- Add tasks via form (trim empty input; default priority: medium; optional due date on create)
- Each task row has an editable `type="date"` input to change `dueDate` after creation
- Priority badges: High (red), Medium (amber), Low (green)
- Checkbox toggles completion; completed rows use `.completed` (strikethrough, muted)
- Live counters: **active** (`!completed`) and **completed** (`completed`)

## DOM and security

- Cache element refs at top of `app.js` (`#task-form`, `#task-input`, `#task-list`, etc.)
- Build list items with `document.createElement` and set user text via **`textContent`**, never `innerHTML`
- Keep `aria-label` / `aria-live` on interactive and stats regions

## CSS conventions

- Card layout centered with `max-width: 480px`
- Priority styles via `.priority-badge.high|medium|low`
- System font stack; visible `:focus` outlines on inputs and buttons

## Scope discipline

- Keep changes minimal and scoped to the requested feature
- Avoid adding frameworks, npm, or localStorage unless explicitly requested
